// TestFourBitAdder.pseudo
//
// ADD YOUR CODE. Real, running tests in your language's test framework.
//
// Owed here:
//   - construction test
//   - an exhaustive sweep: all 16 values of A, all 16 of B, both values of
//     Cin - 512 cases - each checked against integer addition.
//
// The expectation, stated once:
//
//     FOR a IN 0..15
//       FOR b IN 0..15
//         FOR cin IN 0..1
//           adder.setA(a); adder.setB(b); adder.setCin(cin)
//           ASSERT (adder.getCout() * 16) + adder.getSum() EQUALS a + b + cin
//
// Note what this catches that a hand-picked set of cases would not: a broken
// carry between bits 2 and 3 only shows up for particular operand pairs.
